qt6: annotate the lifetime of Assimp FBX scope lookups

GetRequiredElement returns an Element owned by sc, never the temporary lookup
string. GCC 14 supports no_dangling; feature-test it for other compilers.
This applies only to the lookup function, leaving other diagnostics enabled.
https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/C_002b_002b-Attributes.html
https://github.com/assimp/assimp/issues/5145#issuecomment-1599436595

--- a/qtquick3d/src/3rdparty/assimp/src/code/AssetLib/FBX/FBXParser.h
+++ b/qtquick3d/src/3rdparty/assimp/src/code/AssetLib/FBX/FBXParser.h
@@ -223,6 +223,12 @@
 bool HasElement( const Scope& sc, const std::string& index );
 
 // extract a required element from a scope, abort if the element cannot be found
+// The result belongs to sc, not to the temporary lookup string.
+#if defined(__has_cpp_attribute)
+#  if __has_cpp_attribute(gnu::no_dangling)
+[[gnu::no_dangling]]
+#  endif
+#endif
 const Element &GetRequiredElement(const Scope &sc, const std::string &index, const Element *element = nullptr);
 
 // extract required compound scope
